# Normalize line endings. Windows dev host, LF in the repository.
#
# Why this file exists: there was no .gitattributes and core.autocrlf was unset,
# so a Windows tool rewrote the working tree to CRLF and git reported ~220 files
# as modified when nothing had actually changed. That churn twice concealed real
# edits sitting underneath it. See commit 178e6c6, which had to make three
# source-drift guards line-ending agnostic for the same reason.
* text=auto eol=lf
